meta {
  name: Broadcasting Auth
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/broadcasting/auth
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: inherit
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  socket_id: 123456.7890123
  channel_name: private-workspaces.{{workspaceId}}.runs
}

docs {
  Authorizes a Reverb/Echo subscription to a private channel. Lives at
  `/api/broadcasting/auth` (no `/v1`) behind `auth:api`, so it takes the
  bearer token — Echo's `authorizer` should send it. GET is accepted too.

  - `socket_id` — the connection's socket id from Reverb.
  - `channel_name` — `private-` plus a channel from `routes/channels.php`:
    `App.Models.User.{userId}`, `workspaces.{workspaceId}.runs`,
    `workspaces.{workspaceId}.runs.{runId}`,
    `workspaces.{workspaceId}.agent-sessions.{sessionId}`,
    `workspaces.{workspaceId}.workflow-builder-sessions.{sessionId}`,
    `workspaces.{workspaceId}.assistant-sessions.{sessionId}`,
    `workspaces.{workspaceId}.assistants.{assistantId}`,
    `workspaces.{workspaceId}.pages.{pageId}`.

  403 when the caller may not join. On success the response is the
  broadcaster's raw payload, not the JSON envelope: `{ auth }` (plus
  `channel_data` for presence channels).
}
